    q: 'Is dentistry a good career in India?',
    a: 'It depends on how you enter and what you build afterward. Dentistry offers a shorter formal training runway than medicine, real government routes, and a genuinely growing cosmetic and dental-tourism segment. But the base BDS market is oversupplied in cities, MDS specialisation is genuinely competitive (roughly 4-5 candidates per seat), and fresher income is modest (₹20,000-40,000/month) until a patient base or specialisation is built over several years. It rewards people who specialise, differentiate, or practise where competition is lower — a plain BDS with no further plan is a weaker bet than it looks on paper.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Is BDS a backup for students who miss the NEET cutoff for MBBS?',
