  },
  {
    q: 'How much does a BDS graduate actually earn in India?',
    a: 'Fresh BDS graduates in salaried clinic roles or corporate dental chains typically start around ₹20,000-40,000 a month (roughly ₹2.4-4.8 lakh a year). An established solo or partnership private practice built over 5+ years in a metro or Tier-1 city can exceed ₹1 lakh a month, with strong outliers well above that — but that figure describes an experienced practice with a built patient base, not a fresh graduate\'s entry income.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Is there really an oversupply of dentists in India?',
    a: 'Yes, in a specific and honest sense. India has 329-333 dental colleges producing roughly 27,600-27,700 BDS graduates a year, heavily weighted toward private and deemed colleges. Metro and Tier-1 cities have real clinic-density saturation, while smaller towns and semi-urban areas often still have a genuine patient-access gap. It is a distribution and specialisation problem as much as a raw headcount problem.',
